ims3/default/strip/false/crop/1920x1209+0+0/resize/1600/quality/85/format/jpeg/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F74%2F47%2Fd122ddd94efaa3cc64d5b835aab1%2Fsienna-miller-dominic-west.jpg 1600w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/1920x1209+0+0/resize/1800/quality/85/format/jpeg/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F74%2F47%2Fd122ddd94efaa3cc64d5b835aab1%2Fsienna-miller-dominic-west.jpg 1800w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/1920x1209+0+0/resize/2400/quality/85/format/jpeg/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F74%2F47%2Fd122ddd94efaa3cc64d5b835aab1%2Fsienna-miller-dominic-west.jpg 2400w" data-template="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/1920x1209+0+0/resize/{width}/quality/{quality}/format/{format}/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F74%2F47%2Fd122ddd94efaa3cc64d5b835aab1%2Fsienna-miller-dominic-west.jpg" sizes="(min-width: 1350px) 953px, (min-width: 1025px) calc(100vw - 395px), (min-width: 768px) calc(100vw - 60px), calc(100vw - 30px)" class="img" type="image/jpeg" /&gt;             &lt;img src="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/1920x1209+0+0/resize/1100/quality/50/format/jpeg/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F74%2F47%2Fd122ddd94efaa3cc64d5b835aab1%2Fsienna-miller-dominic-west.jpg" data-template="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/1920x1209+0+0/resize/{width}/quality/{quality}/format/{format}/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F74%2F47%2Fd122ddd94efaa3cc64d5b835aab1%2Fsienna-miller-dominic-west.jpg" class="img" alt="Sienna Miller and Dominic West in HBO&amp;#039;s WAR." fetchpriority="high" /&gt;         &lt;/picture&gt; &lt;/div&gt; &lt;div class="credit-caption"&gt;     &lt;div class="caption-wrap"&gt;         &lt;div class="caption" aria-label="Image caption"&gt;             &lt;p&gt;                 HBO's&lt;strong&gt; &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;War&lt;/em&gt; is intended to be an anthology series about two dueling London law firms. The first season stars Dominic West and Sienna Miller as a high-profile couple in the midst of a &lt;em&gt;very &lt;/em&gt;nasty divorce.                 &lt;b class="credit" aria-label="Image credit"&gt;                                          Justin Downing/Sky/HBO                                      &lt;/b&gt;                 &lt;b class="hide-caption"&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/b&gt;             &lt;/p&gt;         &lt;/div&gt;               &lt;button class="toggle-caption" aria-label=""&gt;               &lt;svg class="icon icon--info"&gt;&lt;use href="#icon-info"&gt;&lt;/use&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;               &lt;b&gt;&lt;/b&gt;                 &lt;abbr title="Toggle Caption" class="toggle-caption__info"&gt;i&lt;/abbr&gt;              &lt;/button&gt;     &lt;/div&gt;       &lt;/div&gt;    &lt;/div&gt;    &lt;p&gt;Dominic West specializes in playing men who feel victimized by the consequences of their own actions. One of his signature lines as Jimmy McNulty on &lt;em&gt;The Wire &lt;/em&gt;was, "What the f*** did I do?" The line was often delivered not in the sense of, "Oh no, what did I &lt;em&gt;do&lt;/em&gt;?" But instead, as an indignant, "Why am I getting yelled at? What did &lt;em&gt;I&lt;/em&gt; do?" And while West's take on then-Prince Charles in &lt;em&gt;The Crown &lt;/em&gt;put him in a completely different setting, he retained that sense of arrogant bafflement, affronted whenever he sensed that he was being perceived as the bad guy.&lt;/p&gt;       &lt;p&gt;In HBO's new series &lt;em&gt;War&lt;/em&gt;, West plays Morgan Henderson — a tech mogul, not a cop or a royal. But he, too, has trouble seeing his own fingerprints on his problems, including his marriage. Morgan is married to Carla Duval (Sienna Miller), an A-list actress whose fame is starting to teeter, inevitably, as she ages. As the first episode begins, they both seem aware that the marriage is on its last legs, but no one has acted — at least not openly — quite yet. Then, at a dinner without Carla where he's receiving an award, he spies a beautiful woman in the crowd. Things progress. Someone acts.&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;div id="resnx-s1-5983443-100" class="bucketwrap internallink mediapromo primary"&gt;             &lt;h4 class="internallink__slug"&gt;Television&lt;/h4&gt;       &lt;h2 class="internallink__title"&gt;The biggest divorce trial in British history is the center of HBO's new series, 'War'&lt;/h2&gt;       &lt;article id="resnx-s1-9947443" class="bucketwrap resaudio" aria-label="audio-module"&gt;&lt;div class="audio-module"&gt;       &lt;h4 class="audio-module-title"&gt;The biggest divorce trial in British history is the center of HBO's new series, 'War'&lt;/h4&gt;    &lt;div class="audio-module-controls-wrap" data-audio='{"uid":"nx-s1-5949984:nx-s1-9947443","available":true,"duration":420,"title":"The biggest divorce trial in British history is the center of HBO\u0027s new series, \u0027War\u0027","audioUrl":"https:\/\/ondemand.npr.org\/anon.npr-mp3\/npr\/me\/2026\/10\/20261001_me_the_biggest_divorce_trial_in_british_history_is_the_center_of_hbo_s_new_series_war.mp3?t=progseg&amp;e=nx-s1-5971886&amp;p=3&amp;seg=4&amp;d=420&amp;size=6732113&amp;sc=siteplayer","storyUrl":"https:\/\/www.npr.org\/2026\/10\/01\/nx-s1-5949984\/the-biggest-divorce-trial-in-british-history-is-the-center-of-hbos-new-series-war","slug":"Television","program":"Morning Edition","affiliation":"","song":"","artist":"","album":"","track":0,"type":"segment","subtype":"other","skipSponsorship":false,"hasAdsWizz":false,"isStreamAudioType":false,"podcastEpisodeRawType":"","podcastEpisodeDerivedPlusType":""}' data-audio-metrics='[]'&gt;         &lt;div class="audio-module-controls audio-module-controls--no-js"&gt;             &lt;a class="audio-module-listen" href="https://ondemand.npr.org/anon.npr-mp3/npr/me/2026/10/20261001_me_the_biggest_divorce_trial_in_british_history_is_the_center_of_h